; regression test: a labelled (non-`local`) `use` fact is exported by `load`, along with the
; symbol declarations it needs. Confirmed mechanically: re-declaring `bool P` only raises
; "already declared bool" if `P` genuinely survived the load (see `add_bool`'s guard) --
; there is no other visible side effect of a bare symbol declaration to check directly.
load load-export-helper
expect "EvalError"
    bool P
true
;;; Proof checked.
